## Technology Stack

GUTS IAM is built using a modern backend-focused stack designed for secure authentication, scalable access control, and efficient system performance.

The system follows a layered architecture with strong emphasis on security, modularity, and extensibility.

---

### Backend

- Java — Core programming language
- Spring Boot — Main framework for building REST APIs
- Spring Security — Handles authentication and authorization workflows
- Hibernate / JPA — ORM layer for database interaction

---

### Authentication & Security

- JWT (JSON Web Tokens) — Stateless authentication mechanism for secure API access
- BCrypt Password Encoding — Secure password hashing
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) — Structured authorization model

---

### Session & Caching

- Redis — Used for caching, session management, and token handling to improve performance and scalability

---

### Database

- MySQL — Primary relational database for storing users, roles, permissions, audit logs, and security data

---

### Email Services

- SMTP Email Service — Used for:
  - Email verification during user registration
  - Password reset and account recovery flows

---

### API Design

- RESTful APIs — Standard communication layer between client and server
- JSON — Primary data exchange format

---

### Build & Dependency Management

- Maven — Dependency management and build automation tool

---

### Testing

- JUnit — Unit testing framework for backend validation

---

### Version Control

- Git — Source code version control
- GitHub — Repository hosting and collaboration platform
